From: Daniele Masato <daniele.masato@pm.me>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: gadget: read DTXFSTS by endpoint index

DTXFSTSn belongs to IN endpoint n, not to TX FIFO n. With dedicated FIFOs
the gadget picks the smallest free FIFO that fits, so an endpoint's FIFO
number can differ from its endpoint number. In PIO mode (g_dma = false, as
on the Sophgo CV18xx) dwc2_hsotg_write_fifo() then reads another
endpoint's free space, writes nothing, and re-arms the TX FIFO empty
interrupt forever. On the NanoKVM Lite the mass storage bulk IN endpoint
(ep6in on FIFO 2) never sent data and raised ~46000 interrupts a second.

Same change as Minas Harutyunyan's 2017 "usb: dwc2: Use ep->index in
context of FIFO registers", which was not merged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
@@ -562,7 +562,7 @@
 		}
 	} else if (hsotg->dedicated_fifos && hs_ep->index != 0) {
 		can_write = dwc2_readl(hsotg,
-				       DTXFSTS(hs_ep->fifo_index));
+				       DTXFSTS(hs_ep->index));
 
 		can_write &= 0xffff;
 		can_write *= 4;
@@ -3299,7 +3299,7 @@
 
 	if (!hsotg->dedicated_fifos)
 		return;
-	size = (dwc2_readl(hsotg, DTXFSTS(ep->fifo_index)) & 0xffff) * 4;
+	size = (dwc2_readl(hsotg, DTXFSTS(ep->index)) & 0xffff) * 4;
 	if (size < ep->fifo_size)
 		dwc2_hsotg_txfifo_flush(hsotg, ep->fifo_index);
 }
